SUMMARY: Two confirmed bugs in the current HEAD: a ByteBuf memory leak in transactional bucket equality checks and a broken entry set contains check in RedissonMap.

POINTS:
- [redisson/src/main/java/org/redisson/transaction/RedissonTransactionalBucket.java:404] ByteBuf memory leak in isEquals() finally block: readableBytes() called instead of release() — fix: replace valueBuf.readableBytes(); oldValueBuf.readableBytes(); with valueBuf.release(); oldValueBuf.release();
- [redisson/src/main/java/org/redisson/RedissonMap.java:1861] entrySet().contains() always returns false for valid entries: compares value against Map.Entry object instead of e.getValue() — fix: replace return value != null && value.equals(e); with return value != null && value.equals(e.getValue());

